{
  "_about": "v100: typical weight of each calendar event = how much a normal day's sales usually change while the event runs (percent). Starting values confirmed by the owner (see status); edit freely. Used ONLY when events share dates: on a shared day the stronger event (larger weight, up or down) carries the lift and weaker ones add other_share of theirs. A weaker event keeps its typical value until its own days give enough evidence; from then on the tenant's own data takes over. overlap.prior_days = how many 'days of evidence' the typical value is worth (higher = trusts the typical value longer); data_min_share / data_full_share = below the first the row shows 'Typical value', between the two 'Your data and typical value', above the second 'Your data'; early_min_share = least share of own evidence for an Early signal; max_rows = most 'typical effect' rows in the summary; enabled=false switches the overlap logic off. match = regular expression on the event name without year and 'Phase n'. Countries are matched by code, name or alias. impact_big / impact_notable = the effect (%) from which the event table says 'Big boost' / 'Boost'; the same size downward says 'Slows sales'.",
  "status": "Confirmed by Jerry 2026-10-24 (starting values; edit freely)",
  "overlap": {
    "enabled": true,
    "other_share": 0.25,
    "prior_days": 2.0,
    "data_min_share": 0.3,
    "data_full_share": 0.7,
    "early_min_share": 0.5,
    "max_rows": 8,
    "impact_big": 50,
    "impact_notable": 15
  },
